# Dashboard / portal UI — do not change unless asked

When the user task is about **search**, **import**, **Supabase**, **data**, **RLS**, or **bugs**:

- **Do not edit** layout, spacing, colors, typography, sidebar chrome, table shells, or filter panel styling in the files matched by this rule.
- **Do not introduce** new layout wrappers (`DashboardPageShell`, grid redesigns, motion wrappers) unless the user explicitly requests UI changes.
- **Preserve** the canonical dashboard UI frozen on `main` at commit `1d63582` (see `docs/UI_CANONICAL_ROUTES.md`).
- **Never re-add** applicant `EnterpriseApplicantProfile`, `ApplicantProfile.tsx`, or `OldApplicantWelcomeModal`.

Allowed without explicit UI approval:

- Bug fixes that do not change visual design
- New routes/nav items that match existing sidebar style
- Service/hook/RPC wiring behind existing components

If UI must change: user must say so explicitly (e.g. "change the admin dashboard UI").

Do not edit marketing pages when working on dashboards. See `marketing-website-protected.mdc`.
